{"nodes":[{"id":"evolve_eq_false_of_outside_cone","region":"P1","lean_name":"evolve_eq_false_of_outside_cone","description":"Outside the light cone, nothing happens: after t steps every cell farther than t from the origin is still white.","deps":[],"status":"proved","size":"M","proof_file":"Rule30/Proofs/EvolveEqFalseOfOutsideCone.lean","attempts":[{"identity":"Vesper","session_id":"781795c6-7032-4460-af84-0d2ea53012d9","model":"sonnet","started":"2026-09-05T22:24:51Z","ended":"2026-09-05T22:46:24Z","outcome":"proved","estimate":"M","reported":true,"cost_usd":0.7975254000000002,"turns":27,"notes":"VERIFIED. Axioms: propext, Quot.sound"}],"verified":"2026-09-05T22:46:24Z"},{"id":"evolve_left_edge","region":"P1","lean_name":"evolve_left_edge","description":"The left edge is always black: the cell at -t after t steps is black for every t.","deps":["evolve_eq_false_of_outside_cone"],"status":"proved","size":"M","proof_file":"Rule30/Proofs/EvolveLeftEdge.lean","attempts":[{"identity":"Vesper","session_id":"e429d3ea-1f6a-407b-ba30-688470ae8285","model":"sonnet","started":"2026-09-06T01:01:42Z","ended":"2026-09-06T01:07:18Z","outcome":"proved","estimate":"M","reported":true,"cost_usd":0.36769779999999996,"turns":10,"notes":"VERIFIED. Axioms: propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound"}],"verified":"2026-09-06T01:07:18Z"},{"id":"evolve_right_edge","region":"P1","lean_name":"evolve_right_edge","description":"The right edge is always black: the cell at t after t steps is black for every t.","deps":["evolve_eq_false_of_outside_cone"],"status":"proved","size":"M","proof_file":"Rule30/Proofs/EvolveRightEdge.lean","attempts":[{"identity":"Cadence","session_id":"232ab5d1-dd60-43c1-b32e-a755d7743f2c","model":"sonnet","started":"2026-09-06T14:48:01Z","ended":"2026-09-06T14:49:37Z","outcome":"proved","estimate":"M","reported":true,"cost_usd":0.18280379999999996,"turns":9,"notes":"VERIFIED. Axioms: propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound"}],"verified":"2026-09-06T14:49:37Z"},{"id":"evolve_left_second_diagonal","region":"P1","lean_name":"evolve_left_second_diagonal","description":"The second diagonal from the left is all black: the cell at -t after t+1 steps is black.","deps":["evolve_eq_false_of_outside_cone","evolve_left_edge"],"status":"proved","size":"M","proof_file":"Rule30/Proofs/EvolveLeftSecondDiagonal.lean","attempts":[{"identity":"Vesper","session_id":"9015a7ac-ec03-4e50-b590-82f95dbded57","model":"sonnet","started":"2026-09-06T01:32:37Z","ended":"2026-09-06T01:34:02Z","outcome":"rate_limited","estimate":"M","reported":false,"cost_usd":0.2629998,"turns":11,"notes":"the five-hour window is rate limiting; resume session 9015a7ac-ec03-4e50-b590-82f95dbded57"},{"identity":"Vesper","session_id":"5df887a3-1782-4a5a-a59a-8c68e011d490","model":"sonnet","started":"2026-09-06T01:52:52Z","ended":"2026-09-06T01:53:41Z","outcome":"proved","estimate":"S","reported":true,"cost_usd":0.18189360000000002,"turns":9,"notes":"VERIFIED. Axioms: propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound"}],"verified":"2026-09-06T01:53:41Z"},{"id":"evolve_left_third_diagonal","region":"P1","lean_name":"evolve_left_third_diagonal","description":"The third diagonal from the left is all white: the cell at -t after t+2 steps is white.","deps":["evolve_left_edge","evolve_left_second_diagonal"],"status":"proved","size":"M","proof_file":"Rule30/Proofs/EvolveLeftThirdDiagonal.lean","attempts":[{"identity":"Vesper","session_id":"614c8a2a-978e-4e11-b24e-7379047ef607","model":"sonnet","started":"2026-09-06T14:47:45Z","ended":"2026-09-06T14:49:46Z","outcome":"proved","estimate":"S","reported":true,"cost_usd":0.3178702,"turns":8,"notes":"VERIFIED. Axioms: propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound"}],"verified":"2026-09-06T14:49:46Z"},{"id":"centerColumn_zero","region":"P2","lean_name":"centerColumn_zero","description":"The centre column starts black: the initial configuration has exactly one black cell, at the origin.","deps":[],"status":"proved","size":"S","proof_file":"Rule30/Proofs/CenterColumnZero.lean","attempts":[{"identity":"Emmy","session_id":"a3985ae1-b2c7-4b7f-9e38-66ae94a41618","model":"haiku","started":"2026-09-05T21:33:04Z","ended":"2026-09-05T21:33:58Z","outcome":"proved","estimate":"S","reported":true,"cost_usd":0.108113,"turns":9,"notes":"VERIFIED. Axioms: propext — proof file later deleted by a verify_test fixture sharing its name (race, 2026-09-05); node reopened for re-proof"},{"identity":"Emmy","session_id":"b4af88a7-54f1-47d1-9b25-f4c2a0be464e","model":"haiku","started":"2026-09-05T22:16:19Z","ended":"2026-09-05T22:21:00Z","outcome":"proved","estimate":"S","reported":true,"cost_usd":0.07094610000000001,"turns":9,"notes":"VERIFIED. Axioms: propext"}],"verified":"2026-09-05T22:21:00Z"},{"id":"centerColumnDensity_nonneg","region":"P2","lean_name":"centerColumnDensity_nonneg","description":"The density is never negative: it is a count divided by a natural.","deps":[],"status":"proved","size":"S","proof_file":"Rule30/Proofs/CenterColumnDensityNonneg.lean","attempts":[{"identity":"Emmy","session_id":"90bec323-c76a-4ce2-a96e-b8d28d3db166","model":"haiku","started":"2026-09-06T01:32:57Z","ended":"2026-09-06T01:46:04Z","outcome":"proved","estimate":"S","reported":true,"cost_usd":0.18899090000000002,"turns":20,"notes":"VERIFIED. Axioms: propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound"}],"verified":"2026-09-06T01:46:04Z"},{"id":"centerColumnDensity_le_one","region":"P2","lean_name":"centerColumnDensity_le_one","description":"The density never exceeds one: the filtered set is a subset of range N, so its cardinality is at most N.","deps":[],"status":"proved","size":"M","proof_file":"Rule30/Proofs/CenterColumnDensityLeOne.lean","attempts":[{"identity":"Emmy","session_id":"e7253e46-69f7-45e7-b077-0df129a59929","model":"sonnet","started":"2026-09-06T01:32:57Z","ended":"2026-09-06T01:33:48Z","outcome":"proved","estimate":"M","reported":true,"cost_usd":0.18802839999999998,"turns":8,"notes":"VERIFIED. Axioms: propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound"}],"verified":"2026-09-06T01:33:48Z"},{"id":"centerColumnDensity_succ","region":"P2","lean_name":"centerColumnDensity_succ","description":"The density recurrence: the count of black cells among the first N+1 equals the count among the first N plus one if cell N is black.","deps":[],"status":"proved","size":"M","proof_file":"Rule30/Proofs/CenterColumnDensitySucc.lean","attempts":[{"identity":"Emmy","session_id":"56a7d95a-8260-43c6-987a-f22e25aadb54","model":"sonnet","started":"2026-09-06T01:33:48Z","ended":"2026-09-06T01:51:11Z","outcome":"proved","estimate":"M","reported":true,"cost_usd":0.5431585999999999,"turns":23,"notes":"VERIFIED. Axioms: propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound"}],"verified":"2026-09-06T01:51:11Z"},{"id":"evolve_left_diagonal_recurrence","region":"P1","lean_name":"evolve_left_diagonal_recurrence","description":"One step of rule 30 in diagonal coordinates: the cell one further along the (m+2)-th left diagonal is the diagonal two shallower, xor (the diagonal one shallower or its own previous term). The dictionary every later diagonal proof should cite instead of re-deriving the coordinate shift. One unfold of evolve_succ and rule30_eq; no induction.","deps":[],"status":"proved","size":"S","proof_file":"Rule30/Proofs/EvolveLeftDiagonalRecurrence.lean","attempts":[{"identity":"Vesper","session_id":"4f68a992-563c-4d11-a59b-58de21f8f677","model":"haiku","started":"2026-09-06T15:04:52Z","ended":"2026-09-06T15:18:09Z","outcome":"proved","estimate":"S","reported":true,"cost_usd":0.1586898,"turns":9,"notes":"VERIFIED. Axioms: propext, Quot.sound"}],"verified":"2026-09-06T15:18:09Z"},{"id":"evolve_left_fourth_diagonal","region":"P1","lean_name":"evolve_left_fourth_diagonal","description":"The fourth diagonal from the left alternates black and white with no prefix: evolve (t+3) (-t) = decide (t % 2 = 0). The first non-constant diagonal, and the first node where the recurrence feeds a diagonal its own previous term, so it needs an induction on t rather than a single unfold.","deps":["evolve_left_diagonal_recurrence","evolve_left_second_diagonal","evolve_left_third_diagonal"],"status":"proved","size":"M","proof_file":"Rule30/Proofs/EvolveLeftFourthDiagonal.lean","attempts":[{"identity":"Vesper","session_id":"eb0653fa-59cf-4c72-ab44-5fc55b3c5fce","model":"sonnet","started":"2026-09-06T15:18:09Z","ended":"2026-09-06T15:22:05Z","outcome":"proved","estimate":"M","reported":true,"cost_usd":0.49336860000000005,"turns":10,"notes":"VERIFIED. Axioms: propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound"}],"verified":"2026-09-06T15:22:05Z"},{"id":"evolve_left_fifth_diagonal","region":"P1","lean_name":"evolve_left_fifth_diagonal","description":"The fifth diagonal from the left is all black. Constant again, one step past the alternating one: the recurrence reduces it to d4(j) = d3(j) or d4(j-1), which stays true once true. Evidence that the family cannot be read off by extrapolating the periods.","deps":["evolve_left_diagonal_recurrence","evolve_left_third_diagonal","evolve_left_fourth_diagonal"],"status":"proved","size":"M","proof_file":"Rule30/Proofs/EvolveLeftFifthDiagonal.lean","attempts":[{"identity":"Cadence","session_id":"bb187f03-9ebe-4d24-b72c-fe2054e3fbae","model":"sonnet","started":"2026-09-06T15:22:05Z","ended":"2026-09-06T15:35:09Z","outcome":"proved","estimate":"M","reported":true,"cost_usd":0.273942,"turns":10,"notes":"VERIFIED. Axioms: propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound"}],"verified":"2026-09-06T15:35:09Z"},{"id":"evolve_right_second_diagonal","region":"P1","lean_name":"evolve_right_second_diagonal","description":"The second diagonal from the right alternates, where the second from the left is constant black. The smallest true statement distinguishing the two sides of the cone: one cell in from two black edges, the sides already disagree.","deps":["evolve_right_edge","evolve_eq_false_of_outside_cone"],"status":"proved","size":"M","proof_file":"Rule30/Proofs/EvolveRightSecondDiagonal.lean","attempts":[{"identity":"Cadence","session_id":"3a1659f4-313f-47a4-9023-7f6b37f8b077","model":"sonnet","started":"2026-09-06T15:04:52Z","ended":"2026-09-06T15:18:23Z","outcome":"proved","estimate":"M","reported":true,"cost_usd":0.36346100000000003,"turns":15,"notes":"VERIFIED. Axioms: propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound"}],"verified":"2026-09-06T15:18:23Z"},{"id":"evolve_left_fourth_diagonal_isEventuallyPeriodic","region":"P1","lean_name":"evolve_left_fourth_diagonal_isEventuallyPeriodic","description":"The fourth left diagonal satisfies IsEventuallyPeriodic, the predicate Rule30/Prize.lean states the aperiodicity conjecture with. Bears nothing on that conjecture, which is about the centre column; it gives the predicate its first inhabited instance in the project. Immediate from the closed form with p = 2 and N = 0.","deps":["evolve_left_fourth_diagonal"],"status":"proved","size":"S","proof_file":"Rule30/Proofs/EvolveLeftFourthDiagonalIsEventuallyPeriodic.lean","attempts":[{"identity":"Vesper","session_id":"3693ec06-5a65-4748-abe1-787d76e1df40","model":"haiku","started":"2026-09-06T15:22:05Z","ended":"2026-09-06T15:35:17Z","outcome":"proved","estimate":"S","reported":true,"cost_usd":0.1677569,"turns":17,"notes":"VERIFIED. Axioms: propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound"}],"verified":"2026-09-06T15:35:17Z"},{"id":"evolve_left_diagonals_isEventuallyPeriodic","region":"P1","lean_name":"evolve_left_diagonals_isEventuallyPeriodic","description":"Every left diagonal is eventually periodic. The target the diagonal lemmas are steps towards, and the first node in this DAG that is a goal rather than a step. Not a prize conjecture: it concerns the edge of the cone, not the centre. Measured to k = 63 and no further, with the onset growing in k. Do not dispatch; decompose.","deps":["evolve_left_diagonal_recurrence","evolve_left_fifth_diagonal","evolve_left_fourth_diagonal_isEventuallyPeriodic"],"status":"open","size":"wall","proof_file":null,"attempts":[],"verified":null}]}
